                <pb facs="0312" n="1362" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v11p2/pg1362"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">690D.91/10–554: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The United States Representative at the United
                        Nations</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Lodge</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Department of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">New
                                York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-10-05T16:00:00-05:00">October 5, 1954—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>252. Re Kashmir. As Department suggested USUN,
                    spoke with Zafrulla Khan on Friday,
                    October 1. He said he was informed of Department’s views via Pakistan Foreign
                    Office and suggested further talks after Prime Minister’s departure from New
                    York, possibly 6th.…</p>
                <p>. . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lodge</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
